    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "The MicDao exploit occurred due to a vulnerability in the private _transfer() function. This function burned MicDao tokens whenever triggered, allowing the attacker to artificially reduce the total supply and inflate the token price.\" Vulnerable code snippet: Attack tx: Analysis: CertiK Alert on Twitter / X ChainAegis on Twitter / X"
    },
    {
      "source": "SlowMist",
      "text": "MicDao suffered from a flash loan attack. The attacker gained $12,263. Contract address: 0xf6876f6AB2637774804b85aECC17b434a2B57168."
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "MicDao on BNB Chain was exploited on 2023-10-18 through a DODO flash loan and repeated helper contracts that cycled through a fixed-rate MicDao swap path, producing about $13,000 in loss and 12,260.251676860937684429 USDT in attacker profit. MicDao's intermediary swap path used a fixed internal pricing rule and a per-address swap cap that could be bypassed by creating fresh helper contracts for each call. A burn-on-transfer rule on direct pair transfers also let the attacker skew pool accounting while keeping the profitable leg on the helper path."
    }
  ],
